@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# ELXVRO Blocks v0.37.3 — Play Console Compatibility Audit
+
+- Android 15/16 edge-to-edge remains explicitly enabled via Flutter `SystemUiMode.edgeToEdge` and native `WindowCompat.setDecorFitsSystemWindows(window, false)`; no deprecated status/navigation bar color setters in the compiled MainActivity.
+- A high-level AndroidX edge-to-edge helper was tested and REJECTED: R8 inlined deprecated system bar color setters into the compiled MainActivity. The release retains the verified-safe path.
+- Reduced decode sizes for animal/world icons, board special gems, material tiles, and material shards to lower image-cache memory usage. No images or gameplay assets were removed.
+- Verified normal game, falling blocks, all 300 Adventure levels and original classic-theme menus remain in the release source.
+- Includes new regression tests for edge-to-edge, display-size decoding and progression/service preservation.
+- Preserves package identity and Play Games/billing integration, with an incremented Android versionCode (101).
+
+## Google Play Console note
+The supplied screenshot shows production versionCode 70 (v0.29.6), not versionCode 100 (v0.37.2) or this release. Play Console recommendations for old production releases remain visible until a newer bundle is uploaded to a track and analyzed. Android Play Services may embed its own BitmapFactory image loader; the app's Flutter image-cache changes do not guarantee that Play Console's warning for third-party code will disappear. Inspect the refreshed report after uploading v0.37.3 AAB.
